    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been feeling unusually high or overly excited lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Well, I wouldn't say \"unusually high,\" Doctor. I mean, I've always been a cheerful sort of fellow. But... well, I suppose there have been some mornings lately where I just wake up feeling real, real good. Like the whole valley is just opening right up for me, you know? And I'll catch myself just grinning at absolutely nothing. I hope that doesn't sound too strange? It's just a nice feeling. \n\nBut, um... well, I guess I should mention, since you're asking, that I have been a little... touchy, maybe? Just a bit. Like, if one of the hired hands questions how I'm doing things, or if my wife tells me I need to slow down, I... well, I snap at them. Like they've insulted the family name or something. I always feel terrible about it after, I really do. I'm not a mean person, Doctor, I promise. I don't know why I get so fired up. Does that make sense? I hope I'm answering your question the way you need me to.",
