    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been needing much less sleep than usual?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S036",
      "patient_response": "Well, you know how it is on a farm, Doctor. There's always a lot of chores to be done. I don't want you to think I'm neglecting my health or anything—I've always been an early riser and a hard worker. \n\nBut... well, I suppose lately I haven't been needing quite as much shut-eye as I used to. Most nights, I just kind of doze off in my armchair for maybe two or three hours. And some nights, to be perfectly honest, I don't sleep at all. But I don't feel tired, I promise! I'm up way before the sun, feeling completely charged up and ready to work the whole place like nothing even happened. \n\nI've been getting a lot done, actually, so I thought it was a good thing. But... well, my wife worries it's not right to run on so little rest. I hope I'm not doing something wrong by staying up like that? Is that the kind of information you needed me to tell you?",
